---
intent: >
  Rewrite `.claude/commands/aide/brain.md` so the Mode 2 (config) flow speaks
  the post-collapse `BrainState` contract — four states, no retired fields,
  `.aide/config/brain.aide` everywhere — and so it closes the wiring loop by
  having the agent invoke sync via Bash (launcher recovered from
  `.mcp.json["mcpServers"]["aide"]`) instead of punting the user to a
  separate terminal. Mode 1 (general brain interaction) is preserved unchanged
  in spirit; only its prose touches Mode 2 terminology where they overlap.
---

## Project Structure

This plan rewrites a single command-prompt file. The scope directory is
`.claude/commands/aide/`. Every file inside the scope directory after this
plan executes:

```
.claude/commands/aide/
├── brain.aide                       ← (existing) intent spec governing brain.md
├── brain.md                         ← (modified) command prompt — Mode 1 preserved, Mode 2 rewritten to the four-state contract + agent-invoked sync
└── plan.aide                        ← (new, this file) implementation plan for the brain.md rewrite
```

No new files inside this directory; no deletions. The siblings in
`.claude/commands/aide/` (other command prompts, e.g. `align.md`, `build.md`,
`fix.md`, `plan.md`, `qa.md`, `refactor.md`, `research.md`, `spec.md`,
`synthesize.md`, `update-playbook.md`, `upgrade.md`, the orchestrator `aide.md`)
are out of scope and untouched. Files outside `.claude/commands/aide/` (the
sync CLI under `src/cli/sync/`, the MCP tool descriptions in `src/index.ts`,
the methodology doc at `.aide/docs/brain-aide.md`) are tracked separately and
explicitly NOT planned here.

